    "synthesis": {
      "model_calls": 1,
      "phase": "synthesis",
      "plan": {
        "A": "Own the fastest measured baseline: candidate 73efb39e (0.0098503 s). Refine only its streaming O(N²), O(SN+N) ring-buffer design. Profile/measure parser and allocation costs; a promising safe variant is uninitialized contiguous ring storage because every slot is written before it is read, while keeping zero-initialized 64-bit column sums. Compare buffer sizes, pointer-ring versus modulo indexing, and tight scalar horizontal scans. Keep 64-bit accumulators and exact input/output semantics; submit only independently measured wins over 73ef.",
        "B": "Investigate ARM64-specific improvements starting from the proven streaming algorithm, not from assumed additive changes. Isolate NEON widening add/replace of four int cells into 64-bit column sums, compiler auto-vectorization/restrict alternatives, and a correct blocked NEON prefix scan for the recurrence in the horizontal rolling sum. Candidate 9a3f0504 validates that its repaired vector prefix is correct but is still slower than A (0.0099168 s), so quantify each component end-to-end and retain nothing merely because it is SIMD. Preserve 64-bit mathematical sums and scalar tails for every N,S.",
        "C": "Explore genuinely distinct parallel/memory tradeoffs. The full separable horizontal-strip plus column-chunk approach is valid but its best measurement (0.0103427 s) trails the streaming winner, while the other OpenMP design is much worse (0.0560572 s); treat per-row synchronization and full-matrix storage as likely regressions. Test at most a single-region, thread-owned-column implementation with buffered input and a defensible generic small-work fallback, including allocation and end-to-end costs. Do not adopt fixed test-specific thresholds, unsafe 32-bit intermediate arithmetic, or parallelism that cannot beat A across valid inputs.",
        "G": "Integrate conservatively: begin with the exact fastest admissible A program (73efb39e), and cherry-pick only a change whose combined build, full correctness checks, and repeated timing beat that exact base. Do not combine A/B/C ideas on faith: parser, allocation, SIMD, and OpenMP effects may overlap or regress. Require standard-input parsing of signed integers, 64-bit window/column accumulation, correct negative-only maxima, ring overwrite only after initialization, and the required single numeric output. If no integration is measurably faster, deliver candidate 73ef unchanged.",
        "analysis": "The baseline is 0.1335898 s; all admissible programs replace its O(SN²) serpentine updates with O(N²) rolling box sums, yielding about 13.6x speedup. The fastest observed program is A/73efb39e at 0.0098503 s, narrowly ahead of the other streaming variants; therefore data movement and parsing, rather than another algorithmic rewrite, are the main low-risk opportunities. ARM64 NEON produced only a small deficit, and observed OpenMP/full-matrix variants are slower, so integration should favor the compact sequential streaming design unless a complete measured candidate proves otherwise."
      },
